## Verify Configuration Before Boot

Before booting compute nodes, verify that BSS and cloud-init are configured
correctly. These checks catch the most common failures before a wasted boot
cycle.

First, confirm that BSS has the correct kernel parameters stored:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Verify BSS boot params are uploaded -->
```bash
ochami -k bss boot params get \
	| grep -q "ds=nocloud-net" \
	&& echo "BSS: OK" \
	|| { echo "BSS: FAILED - check boot params"; exit 1; }
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

Next, confirm that the cloud-init default configuration was uploaded
successfully:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Verify cloud-init defaults are uploaded -->
```bash
ochami -k cloud-init defaults get \
	| grep -q "base-url" \
	&& echo "cloud-init defaults: OK" \
	|| { echo "cloud-init defaults: FAILED"; exit 1; }
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

Finally, confirm that the compute group cloud-init configuration is present.
This is what delivers the SSH keys and munge key to the node at boot:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Verify cloud-init compute group is uploaded -->
```bash
ochami -k cloud-init group get raw compute \
	| grep -q "compute" \
	&& echo "cloud-init group: OK" \
	|| { echo "cloud-init group: FAILED"; exit 1; }
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

Finally, confirm that the cloud-init server resolves each compute node by its
IP address. This is the lookup the node itself performs at boot, and the only
check here that has to run after node discovery.

The server answers `/cloud-init/meta-data` from an in-memory map of SMD's
Ethernet interfaces that it refreshes on a timer, so a node registered a moment
ago is not visible to it yet. A node that boots into that window gets no
cloud-init data at all, which means no root SSH key and no munge key, and it
never becomes reachable. Wait for the lookup to succeed before powering the
nodes on.

The request below is the one the node will send. `X-Forwarded-For` carries the
node's address so that the server resolves the same entry; haproxy appends its
own entry to the header and the server reads the first.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Verify the cloud-init server resolves each compute node -->
```bash
for ((i=0; i<num_computes; i++)); do
	for ((t=0; ; t++)) ; do
		curl -fsS -o /dev/null \
			-H "X-Forwarded-For: ${c_ip[$i]}" \
			"http://${sms_ip}:8081/cloud-init/meta-data" && break
		(( t < 18 )) || {
			echo "cloud-init node: FAILED for ${c_name[$i]}"
			exit 1
		}
		echo "Waiting for cloud-init to resolve ${c_name[$i]}..."
		sleep 5
	done
done
echo "cloud-init node: OK"
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
